agraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An async closure that takes the error from the upstream and returns a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" to be fully consumed for side effects before retrying."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"text":" that emits the same elements as the upstream but retries on failure using the given strategy,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performing the transformation before each retry.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The provided transformation closure is executed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" each retry, allowing for side effects such as refreshing tokens or resetting state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The closure’s returned ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always fully consumed before the retry occurs, but its elements are ignored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The element type of the returned sequence does not need to match the upstream’s element type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for performing asynchronous side effects like credential refresh before retrying the main sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example-Refreshing-an-access-token-on-a-401-HTTP-error-before-retrying-the-main-request","text":"Example: Refreshing an access token on a 401 HTTP error before retrying the main request","type":"heading","level":2},{"code":["let mainRequest = URLSession.shared.dataTaskAsyncSequence(for: URLRequest(url: URL(string: \"https:\/\/api.example.com\/da